
# Project 4: Power Pivot, DAX & Data Modelling

## Project Overview
This project demonstrates how to build a relational data model in Excel using Power Pivot, create relationships between multiple tables, and perform business analysis using DAX measures.

## Project Objectives
- Create and manage multiple related data tables.
- Understand primary keys and foreign keys.
- Load data into the Power Pivot Data Model.
- Establish relationships between Customers, Products, and Sales.
- Refresh and update the data model dynamically.
- Create DAX measures for sales and quantity analysis.
- Integrate data from multiple sources.
- Build interactive dashboards using PivotTables and PivotCharts.
- Apply DAX functions such as CALCULATE, SUM, and COUNT.

## Workbook Structure

| Worksheet | Description |
|---|---|
| Customers | Customer information and city details |
